        "message": "Extend the Sensors override to the second coupling wait: skip the ECM update when the render thread has not consumed it\n\nsensors-override-pair-on-1 (on-arm lethal, witness, override loaded and\nverified) still tripped command_expired at the goal-approach turn: ONE\n106.1 ms physics stall (sim 50.200 -> 50.202), the controller\nrepublishing the frozen stamp 50.200 at 40 Hz, and the camera frame at\n50.2 never captured \u2014 the same class, now isolated to the SECOND\nrender/physics coupling wait in Sensors::PostUpdate: updateTimeCv,\nwhich blocks the physics thread until the render thread's\nrenderUtil.Update() (the CPU-heavy ECM->scene application at a\nviewpoint change) consumes the pending update. The first wait (arming)\nwas already non-blocking, which is why only one stall remained and the\noff arm's armed window was clean (<30 ms max gap).\n\nThe extension follows the same approved design: when the previous ECM\nupdate is unconsumed, SKIP this cycle's UpdateFromECM instead of\nwaiting. The in-flight render keeps its already-buffered state; the\nnext cycle refreshes from the current ECM; the scene lags at most one\nrender iteration and sensor stamps stay simulation-correct. Patch\nregenerated against the pristine gz-sim8_8.15.0 tag with all hunks,\ndry-run verified."
      },
